                <pb facs="0890" n="800" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg800"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.044/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bailly-Blanchard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-09-20T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 21—11:06
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>67. The President received the Admiral and myself in audience this morning, and
                    finally, after a two hour conference, gave us most formal assurances: <list>
                        <label>1st.</label>
                        <item>That the nine laws which had been passed and promulgated in violation
                            of the agreement of August 24th, 1918, would be repealed.</item>
                        <label>2d.</label>
                        <item>That the law on ammunition and firearms, not promulgated, would so
                            remain, until agreement thereon had been reached by the Government and
                            Legation, and then would be modified immediately after
                            promulgation.</item>
                        <label>3d.</label>
                        <item>That the law to return sequestrated property would be promulgated as
                            passed, being modified immediately thereafter according to the original
                            agreement.</item>
                        <label>4th.</label>
                        <item>That, after agreement on some minor points, the three laws mentioned
                            in my 53, August 20, 11 a.m.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d699-f1"/> would be
                            enacted.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Orders have been issued, in view of the above and in accordance with the
                    Admiral’s program, to pay to the President, Secretaries of State and Members of
                    the Council of State, their suspended salaries for July and August, [thirty]
                    days being given in which program to be fulfilled.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
